Patch summary:
A GPU reset an application causes ends that application, not the VM. When
the host GPU was reset and a guest application's VkDevice was lost,
gfxstream aborted (GFXSTREAM_FATAL "Encountered device lost"), and with it
crosvm and the whole VM: 3DMark Steel Nomad Light on an Intel UHD 770 under
WSL2 faults the GPU in the driver's own memory, and every run took Ika down.

- on_DeviceLost(), called for every guest call that returned
  VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, logs once (with the DeviceLostHelper's diagnosis)
  instead of aborting; the application gets VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST from its
  own calls.
- The VK_CHECKs on guest devices (the Android native buffer queue
  submissions and the QSRI fence wait, the fence pool's reset and create)
  become VK_CHECK_GUEST_DEVICE, which treats VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST as the
  application's and stays fatal for any other failure.
- When gfxstream's own VkDevice is lost (a VK_CHECK of its own work fails
  with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST), its ColorBuffers and display are gone: it
  exits with the code crosvm uses for a guest reboot, 32, so that the VM
  manager restarts the VM instead of it ending.
diff --git a/host/virtio_gpu_gfxstream_renderer.cpp b/host/virtio_gpu_gfxstream_renderer.cpp
index 019b8e6ef..c5c9da54d 100644
--- a/host/virtio_gpu_gfxstream_renderer.cpp
+++ b/host/virtio_gpu_gfxstream_renderer.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ extern "C" {
 #include "gfxstream/virtio-gpu-gfxstream-renderer.h"
 }  // extern "C"
 
+#include <unistd.h>
+
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <optional>
 #include <string_view>
@@ -870,6 +872,12 @@ VG_EXPORT int stream_renderer_init(struct stream_renderer_param* stream_renderer
                             return;
                         }
                         fb->logVulkanDeviceLost();
+                        // gfxstream's own device is gone with the GPU reset, and with it every
+                        // ColorBuffer and the display. Exit with the code crosvm uses for a guest
+                        // reboot, so that the VM manager restarts the VM instead of it ending.
+                        GFXSTREAM_ERROR("gfxstream's VkDevice was lost; exiting with code 32 so "
+                                        "that the VM restarts.");
+                        _exit(32);
                     },
             }));
 
